COMMON BASIC STEPS FOR EVERY ASP.NET PRACTICAL

1. Open Visual Studio
2. Click “Create a new project”
3. Select:
    ASP.NET Web Application (.NET Framework)
4. Click Next
5. Give Project Name
    Example:
    AWT_LINQ
    AWT_MVC
6. Click Create
7. Choose Template:

* Web Forms → for normal ASP.NET practicals
* MVC → for MVC practical

8. Click Create
9. Right Click Project in Solution Explorer
10. Add required files:

* Add → Web Form
* Add → Class
* Add → Controller
* Add → View

11. Write/Paste code
12. Save files
    Shortcut:
    Ctrl + S
13. Run project
    Shortcut:
    Ctrl + F5
14. Browser opens and shows output
15. Check output properly
16. If page not opening:
    Right Click page → Set As Start Page
17. Stop project after completion

COMMON FILES

* .aspx → Web page
* .cs → C# backend code
* Web.config → Configuration
* .sln → Complete project file

COMMON CONTROLS

* TextBox → Input
* Label → Display text
* Button → Click action
* GridView → Show table
* DropDownList → Select options
